IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc1-s7-definitions-and-evidence.l4 -- section 7, subsections (8) to (11): the meaning of "flight" and "in flight", "in service", and the certificates of the Minister of Foreign Affairs.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The periods ("in flight", "in service") are tested on moments the person states: hours on ONE clock (the same zero for every moment; decimals allowed), because (9) counts twenty-four hours.
-- At the instant a period ends the text does not say whether the aircraft is still in flight or in service ("until the later of ... the time at which"): the answer there is NOTHING.
-- Before the period begins, and after it ends, the answer is JUST FALSE ("from the time ... until": a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)).

§ `Section 7(8) -- Definition of flight and in flight`

-- src:517 | Definition of flight and in flight
-- src:518 | (8) For the purposes of this section, of the definition peace officer in section 2 and of sections 27.1, 76 and 77, flight means the act of flying or moving through the air and an aircraft is deemed to be in flight from the time when all external doors are closed following embarkation until the later of
-- src:519 | (a) the time at which any such door is opened for the purpose of disembarkation, and
-- src:520 | (b) where the aircraft makes a forced landing in circumstances in which the owner or operator thereof or a person acting on behalf of either of them is not in control of the aircraft, the time at which control of the aircraft is restored to the owner or operator thereof or a person acting on behalf of either of them.
@ref s 7(8) (src:517-520)
GIVEN `it is the act of flying or moving through the air` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(8) flight` MEANS
    IF `it is the act of flying or moving through the air`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "flight means the act of flying or moving through the air"

@ref s 7(8) (src:517-520)
GIVEN `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment all external doors were closed following embarkation` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment any such door was opened for the purpose of disembarkation, if it has been` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the aircraft made a forced landing in circumstances in which the owner or operator or a person acting on behalf of either of them was not in control of the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the moment control of the aircraft was restored to the owner or operator or a person acting on behalf of either of them, if it has been` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(8) the aircraft is deemed to be in flight` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` LESS THAN `the moment all external doors were closed following embarkation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the time when all external doors are closed following embarkation until the later of"
        IF NOT `the end is known` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the period has not ended: paragraph (a) has not happened, or (b) applies and control has not been restored
        IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` LESS THAN `the end` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` EQUALS `the end` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say whether the aircraft is still in flight at the very moment the door is opened or control is restored
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the later of"
    WHERE
        `the opening` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the moment any such door was opened for the purpose of disembarkation, if it has been`
            WHEN JUST t THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `the restoring` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the moment control of the aircraft was restored to the owner or operator or a person acting on behalf of either of them, if it has been`
            WHEN JUST t THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `the opening is known` MEANS NOT (`the moment any such door was opened for the purpose of disembarkation, if it has been` EQUALS NOTHING)
        `the restoring is known` MEANS NOT (`the moment control of the aircraft was restored to the owner or operator or a person acting on behalf of either of them, if it has been` EQUALS NOTHING)
        `the end is known` MEANS
            `the opening is known`
            AND ((NOT `the aircraft made a forced landing in circumstances in which the owner or operator or a person acting on behalf of either of them was not in control of the aircraft`) OR `the restoring is known`)
        `the end` MEANS
            IF `the aircraft made a forced landing in circumstances in which the owner or operator or a person acting on behalf of either of them was not in control of the aircraft` AND `the restoring` GREATER THAN `the opening`
            THEN `the restoring`
            ELSE `the opening`

-- The answer the other subsections ask for: the aircraft is in flight if it is flying or moving through the air, or is deemed to be in flight.
@ref s 7(8) (src:517-520)
GIVEN `it is flying or moving through the air` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is deemed to be in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(8) the aircraft is in flight` MEANS
    IF `it is flying or moving through the air` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `it is deemed to be in flight, by s 7(8)`

§ `Section 7(9) -- Definition of in service`

-- src:521 | Definition of in service
-- src:522 | (9) For the purposes of this section and section 77, an aircraft shall be deemed to be in service from the time when pre-flight preparation of the aircraft by ground personnel or the crew thereof begins for a specific flight until
-- src:523 | (a) the flight is cancelled before the aircraft is in flight,
-- src:524 | (b) twenty-four hours after the aircraft, having commenced the flight, lands, or
-- src:525 | (c) the aircraft, having commenced the flight, ceases to be in flight,
-- src:526 | whichever is the latest.
@ref s 7(9) (src:521-526)
GIVEN `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment pre-flight preparation of the aircraft by ground personnel or the crew began for a specific flight` IS A NUMBER
      `the moment the flight was cancelled before the aircraft was in flight, if it was` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the moment the aircraft, having commenced the flight, landed, if it has` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the moment the aircraft, having commenced the flight, ceased to be in flight, if it has` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(9) the aircraft is deemed to be in service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` LESS THAN `the moment pre-flight preparation of the aircraft by ground personnel or the crew began for a specific flight` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the time when pre-flight preparation of the aircraft by ground personnel or the crew thereof begins for a specific flight until"
        IF NOT `the end is known` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the period has not ended
        IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` LESS THAN `the end` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the moment asked about, in hours on one clock` EQUALS `the end` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say whether the aircraft is still in service at the very moment the latest of (a), (b) and (c) falls
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whichever is the latest"
    WHERE
        `the cancellation` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the moment the flight was cancelled before the aircraft was in flight, if it was`
            WHEN JUST t THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `the landing` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the moment the aircraft, having commenced the flight, landed, if it has`
            WHEN JUST t THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `the ceasing` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the moment the aircraft, having commenced the flight, ceased to be in flight, if it has`
            WHEN JUST t THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        `it was cancelled` MEANS NOT (`the moment the flight was cancelled before the aircraft was in flight, if it was` EQUALS NOTHING)
        `it landed and ceased` MEANS (NOT (`the moment the aircraft, having commenced the flight, landed, if it has` EQUALS NOTHING)) AND (NOT (`the moment the aircraft, having commenced the flight, ceased to be in flight, if it has` EQUALS NOTHING))
        `the end is known` MEANS `it was cancelled` OR `it landed and ceased`
        `twenty-four hours after the landing` MEANS `the landing` PLUS 24
        `the end` MEANS
            IF `it was cancelled`
            THEN `the cancellation`
            ELSE IF `twenty-four hours after the landing` GREATER THAN `the ceasing` THEN `twenty-four hours after the landing` ELSE `the ceasing`

§ `Section 7(10) and (11) -- Certificates of the Minister of Foreign Affairs`

-- src:527 | Certificate as evidence
-- src:528 | (10) In any proceedings under this Act, a certificate purporting to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs is admissible in evidence without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have signed it and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the facts it states that are relevant to the question of whether any person is a member of United Nations personnel, a member of associated personnel or a person who is entitled under international law to protection from attack or threat of attack against his or her person, freedom or dignity.
@ref s 7(10) (src:527-528)
GIVEN `the certificate is tendered in proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(10) the certificate is admissible in evidence without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have signed it` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is tendered in proceedings under this Act` AND `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings under this Act, a certificate purporting to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs"

@ref s 7(10) (src:528-528)
GIVEN `the certificate is tendered in proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facts it states are relevant to the question of whether any person is a member of United Nations personnel, a member of associated personnel or a person who is entitled under international law to protection from attack or threat of attack against his or her person, freedom or dignity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(10) the certificate is proof of the facts it states` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the certificate is tendered in proceedings under this Act` AND `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate purporting to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs"
        IF NOT `the facts it states are relevant to the question of whether any person is a member of United Nations personnel, a member of associated personnel or a person who is entitled under international law to protection from attack or threat of attack against his or her person, freedom or dignity` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the facts it states that are relevant to the question of whether any person is a member of United Nations personnel, a member of associated personnel or a person who is entitled under international law to protection from attack or threat of attack against his or her person, freedom or dignity"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof of the facts it states"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:529 | Idem
-- src:530 | (11) A certificate purporting to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs stating
-- src:531 | (a) that at a certain time any state was engaged in an armed conflict against Canada or was allied with Canada in an armed conflict,
-- src:532 | (b) that at a certain time any convention, treaty or other international agreement was or was not in force and that Canada was or was not a party thereto, or
-- src:533 | (c) that Canada agreed or did not agree to accept and apply the provisions of any convention, treaty or other international agreement in an armed conflict in which Canada was involved,
-- src:534 | is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it, and is proof of the facts so stated.
@ref s 7(11) (src:529-534)
DECLARE `s 7(11) what the certificate states` IS ONE OF
    `s 7(11)(a) that at a certain time any state was engaged in an armed conflict against Canada or was allied with Canada in an armed conflict`
    `s 7(11)(b) that at a certain time any convention, treaty or other international agreement was or was not in force and that Canada was or was not a party thereto`
    `s 7(11)(c) that Canada agreed or did not agree to accept and apply the provisions of any convention, treaty or other international agreement in an armed conflict in which Canada was involved`
    `s 7(11) something else`

@ref s 7(11) (src:529-534)
GIVEN `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      statement IS A `s 7(11) what the certificate states`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(11) the certificate is admissible in evidence in any proceedings without proof of the signature or authority of the person appearing to have issued it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate purporting to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs"
        IF statement EQUALS `s 7(11) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "stating (a) that at a certain time any state was engaged in an armed conflict against Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 7(11) (src:529-534)
GIVEN `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      statement IS A `s 7(11) what the certificate states`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(11) the certificate is proof of the facts so stated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it purports to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate purporting to have been issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs"
        IF statement EQUALS `s 7(11) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and is proof of the facts so stated"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
